  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 2303.02 Display of Vessel Number",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 2303.02 Display of Vessel Number. Each vessel number issued by the department shall:\n\n(a) Be displayed pursuant to RSA 270-E:8, I;\n\n(b) Have spaces or hyphens that are equal to the width of a letter other than “l” or a number other than “1” between the letter and number groupings;\n\n(c) Be painted on or attached to removable plates that are temporarily yet firmly attached to each side of the forward half of the vessel and clearly visible at all times when the vessel is being used by a manufacturer or dealer for purposes of testing or demonstrating; or\n\n(d) Be painted on or attached to a backing plate that is permanently attached to the forward half of the vessel so that the number is clearly visible from each side of the vessel on antique vessels, classic vessels, or vessels in which the numbers would not be clearly visible on the hull or superstructure.\n\nSource. #5283, eff 11-22-91; ss by #6616, eff 10-25-97, EXPIRED: 10-25-05\n\nNew. #8506, INTERIM, eff 12-7-05, EXPIRES: 6-5-06; ss by #8617, eff 4-28-06, EXPIRED: 1-21-15 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 2300)\n\nNew. #10787, eff 2-20-15; ss by #14321, eff 7-16-25, EXPIRES: 7-16-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c2300.html"
